# 1️⃣ What KafkaErrorConfig REALLY is (mental model first)

Before code, one important correction:

👉 **KafkaErrorConfig itself is NOT DLQ**
👉 It is the **engine that decides what to do when consumer fails**

DLQ is just **one outcome**.

Flow in real systems:

```
Consumer
  ↓
Business logic
  ↓
Exception happens
  ↓
DefaultErrorHandler
  ↓
Retry (in-memory or backoff)
  ↓
Still failing?
  ↓
DeadLetterPublishingRecoverer
  ↓
DLQ topic
```

So your KafkaErrorConfig = **traffic police** 🚦

---

# 2️⃣ DLQ DESIGN (How seniors name & think)

Let’s define topics clearly (this matters in interviews & real ops):

```text
security-match.event.v1          (main topic)
security-match.event.v1.dlq      (dead letter topic)
```

Rule:

* DLQ topic **same partitions as main topic**
* Same key → helps ordering & replay

